        "summary": "Per Ce13, μeff = 8.39 μB at 300 K, decreasing to ~5.6 μB at 2 K, consistent with thirteen weakly or non-coupled f1 ions. Curie–Weiss C = 10.0 cm3 mol−1 K and θ = −33 K (300–90 K); below 90 K the χM−1 plot is more Curie-like with θ near 0 K. Isothermal M vs H shows no saturation; M ≈ 10 NμB at 2 K and 5 T, suggesting very weak to zero intra-cluster exchange plus ligand-field/spin–orbit reduction. Variable-frequency AC susceptibility shows no χM″ maxima, indicating absence of SMM behaviour.",
