        "summary": "Per Pr13, μeff = 12.60 μB at 300 K (calc. 12.9 μB for thirteen weakly coupled f2 ions), decreasing slowly then rapidly below ~100 K to ~4 μB at 2 K. Curie–Weiss C = 21.7 cm3 mol−1 K and θ = −26.5 K. Nearly linear isothermal M vs H plots at 2–3 K reach only ~7.5–7.6 NμB at 5 T, indicating intra-cluster antiferromagnetic coupling plus weak spin–orbit effects and a probable S = 1 ground state. AC susceptibility shows no χM″ maxima (no SMM behaviour).",
